From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mpv-ht development <development@mpv-ht.local>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 17:05:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] gpu-next: refresh paused frames after render option changes

VOCTRL_UPDATE_RENDER_OPTS already requests a redraw, but gpu-next can reuse
libplacebo intermediates cached before the new options were applied.  A paused
frame therefore keeps stale pixels until playback supplies another frame.

Invalidate the renderer cache when options change while paused.  The existing
draw-frame flush path then rebuilds the cached frame with the new options,
without seeking or briefly resuming playback.
---
 video/out/vo_gpu_next.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/video/out/vo_gpu_next.c b/video/out/vo_gpu_next.c
--- a/video/out/vo_gpu_next.c
+++ b/video/out/vo_gpu_next.c
@@ -1227,8 +1227,13 @@ static void update_options(struct vo *vo)
     bool old_dovi_enhancement_layer = p->next_opts->dovi_enhancement_layer;
     bool changed = m_config_cache_update(p->opts_cache);
     changed = m_config_cache_update(p->next_opts_cache) || changed;
-    if (changed)
+    if (changed) {
         update_render_options(vo);
+        // A paused redraw has no new frame to invalidate intermediates that
+        // were produced with the previous render options.
+        if (p->paused)
+            p->flush_cache = true;
+    }
     if (old_dovi_enhancement_layer != p->next_opts->dovi_enhancement_layer)
         p->flush_cache = true;
 
